Rare is an open source alternative for Epic Games Launcher, using '''Legendary''', a command line alternative. It provides a graphical interface written in '''PySide6''', allowing users to manage their games in a more intuitive way. Rare aims to be a lightweight and feature-full experience, integrating seamlessly with Legendary.

== Overview ==
Rare is designed to run natively on most major platforms, providing a native experience for users. It is developed in '''Python''', which enables easy integration with Legendary. The project focuses on being as lightweight as possible while still offering a wide range of features.

=== Features ===
The key features of Rare include:
* Native support for most major platforms
* A lightweight and feature-full experience
* Seamless integration with '''Legendary'''
* Support for packages
* A simple and intuitive interface

== Features ==
Rare offers several features that make it an attractive alternative to the Epic Games Launcher. These include:
* '''Game covers''': Rare allows users to view their games with their respective covers.
* '''Game details''': Users can view detailed information about their games, including settings and updates.
* '''Downloads''': Rare provides a simple way to manage downloads and updates for games.
* '''Application settings''': Users can customize the application to suit their needs.

== Installation ==
Rare can be installed on various platforms. 
=== Windows ===
There is an ''.msi'' installer available for Windows. 
For more information, please visit the [https://github.com/RareDevs/Rare GitHub repository]. 

== Community ==
Rare has a community-driven approach, with a [https://discord.gg/YvmABK9YSk Discord server] available for discussion and support. The project is open source, and contributions are welcome. The '''Rare''' logo was designed by ''@MultisampledNight'' and is licensed under '''CC BY-SA 4.0'''.